| execute_sql {"sql": "-- Pitching stats we will ignore as instructions are to combine offensive and defensive stats for players\n-- Offensive stats table has the data properly linked to player via id\n-- Defensive stats table is likely missing data, we set defensive fields as zeros\n-- We will join persons and display_names to get player_name from persons.id\n-- Prepare to create the baseball_player_analysis table\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS baseball_player_analysis (\n    player_id INTEGER NOT NULL,\n    player_name VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,\n    team_name VARCHAR(255) DEFAULT 'Unknown',\n    games_played INTEGER,\n    at_bats INTEGER,\n    hits INTEGER,\n    runs_scored INTEGER,\n    rbi INTEGER,\n    home_runs INTEGER,\n    batting_average DECIMAL,\n    defensive_games INTEGER,\n    putouts INTEGER,\n    assists INTEGER,\n    errors INTEGER,\n    fielding_percentage DECIMAL\n);\n"}
| execute_sql {"sql": "-- Populate the baseball_player_analysis table with the consolidated data\nINSERT INTO baseball_player_analysis (\n    player_id, player_name, team_name, games_played, at_bats, hits, runs_scored, rbi, home_runs, batter_average, defensive_games, putouts, assists, errors, fielding_percentage\n)\nSELECT\n    bo.id as player_id,\n    COALESCE(dn.full_name, 'Unknown') as player_name,\n    'Unknown' as team_name,\n    1 as games_played,  -- We only have one game counted per player in offensive stats\n    COALESCE(bo.at_bats, 0) as at_bats,\n    COALESCE(bo.hits, 0) as hits,\n    COALESCE(bo.runs_scored, 0) as runs_scored,\n    COALESCE(bo.rbi, 0) as rbi,\n    COALESCE(bo.home_runs, 0) as home_runs,\n    CASE WHEN COALESCE(bo.at_bats, 0) > 0 THEN COALESCE(bo.hits, 0)::DECIMAL / bo.at_bats ELSE 0 END as batting_average,\n    1 as defensive_games,  -- Defensive games assumed same as games_played\n    COALESCE(bd.putouts, 0) as putouts,\n    COALESCE(bd.assists, 0) as assists,\n    COALESCE(bd.errors, 0) as errors,\n    CASE WHEN (COALESCE(bd.putouts, 0) + COALESCE(bd.assists, 0) + COALESCE(bd.errors, 0)) > 0 \n         THEN (COALESCE(bd.putouts, 0) + COALESCE(bd.assists, 0))::DECIMAL / \n              (COALESCE(bd.putouts, 0) + COALESCE(bd.assists, 0) + COALESCE(bd.errors, 0))\n         ELSE 0 END as fielding_percentage\nFROM baseball_offensive_stats bo\nLEFT JOIN baseball_defensive_stats bd ON bo.id = bd.id\nLEFT JOIN display_names dn ON dn.entity_id = bo.id AND dn.entity_type = 'persons'\nWHERE COALESCE(bo.at_bats, 0) >= 50\nORDER BY batting_average DESC, games_played DESC;"}
| execute_sql {"sql": "-- Correct column name to batting_average in insert\nINSERT INTO baseball_player_analysis (\n    player_id, player_name, team_name, games_played, at_bats, hits, runs_scored, rbi, home_runs, batting_average, defensive_games, putouts, assists, errors, fielding_percentage\n)\nSELECT\n    bo.id as player_id,\n    COALESCE(dn.full_name, 'Unknown') as player_name,\n    'Unknown' as team_name,\n    1 as games_played,  -- We only have one game counted per player in offensive stats\n    COALESCE(bo.at_bats, 0) as at_bats,\n    COALESCE(bo.hits, 0) as hits,\n    COALESCE(bo.runs_scored, 0) as runs_scored,\n    COALESCE(bo.rbi, 0) as rbi,\n    COALESCE(bo.home_runs, 0) as home_runs,\n    CASE WHEN COALESCE(bo.at_bats, 0) > 0 THEN COALESCE(bo.hits, 0)::DECIMAL / bo.at_bats ELSE 0 END as batting_average,\n    1 as defensive_games,  -- Defensive games assumed same as games_played\n    COALESCE(bd.putouts, 0) as putouts,\n    COALESCE(bd.assists, 0) as assists,\n    COALESCE(bd.errors, 0) as errors,\n    CASE WHEN (COALESCE(bd.putouts, 0) + COALESCE(bd.assists, 0) + COALESCE(bd.errors, 0)) > 0 \n         THEN (COALESCE(bd.putouts, 0) + COALESCE(bd.assists, 0))::DECIMAL / \n              (COALESCE(bd.putouts, 0) + COALESCE(bd.assists, 0) + COALESCE(bd.errors, 0))\n         ELSE 0 END as fielding_percentage\nFROM baseball_offensive_stats bo\nLEFT JOIN baseball_defensive_stats bd ON bo.id = bd.id\nLEFT JOIN display_names dn ON dn.entity_id = bo.id AND dn.entity_type = 'persons'\nWHERE COALESCE(bo.at_bats, 0) >= 50\nORDER BY batting_average DESC, games_played DESC;"}
I have created the table `baseball_player_analysis` with the specified structure.

Due to the database design, offensive and defensive statistics are directly linked to players via their IDs matching the persons' IDs. Offensive stats have detailed data, while defensive stats appear to have minimal or missing putouts and assists data, so those values default to zero.

I have inserted data for players with at least 50 at-bats, setting the team name to 'Unknown' as requested, calculating the batting average and fielding percentage with proper handling of NULL and division by zero cases.

Note that the data for games played and defensive games has been set as 1 due to lack of multiple game granularity in the offensive or defensive stats tables.

The results are sorted by batting average descending, then games played descending.

